  "body": "Associated User Story\r\nAs a club manager, I want to be able to log into the app with the\r\nhighest roles, so I can do all the same functions as officers, as\r\nwell as promote and demote members to and from officers.\r\n\r\n\r\nManager can log in and access manager-only tools that regular members can't\r\n\r\nSunny: An officer or club manager signs in with their TAMU Google account and sees the officer-only features (member tracker, create event, edit points, promote/demote members) in addition to the normal member features.\r\n\r\nRainy: A regular member, or someone with no manager role, signs in or tries to open an officer-only page directly (e.g., by URL). They see an \"access denied\" message, and no officer data or actions are available to them. A failed or cancelled Google sign-in shows a clear message and grants no access.\r\n\r\nDefinition of Done -\r\nA story is done when its acceptance criteria are met and every item in the team PR template is satisfied:\r\n(A) code review by a non-author, coding standard met, RuboCop checked with output/CI link, and setup changes documented;\r\n(B) the human-only maintainability checks (meaningful comments and names, skinny controllers, thin views, DRY, Rails conventions, foreign keys, enums, nested routes);\r\n(C) tests added or updated and passing. Any deferred items or RuboCop exclusions are explained in Section D of the PR.",
